# The codebase as an ability

`deus eval` evaluates an expression against the codebase; with the `Workspace` ability that
expression can also read and change it (task 10b95384, [D137](../../docs/DECISIONS.md)). An agent
that would chain `deus ls`, `deus view`, an edit and `deus update` sends one snippet instead:

```
deus eval 'List.map (fun n => Workspace.view n) (Workspace.names "Coverage.Spec.")'
```

Written in the order of the process (D92); the laws ran red against a handler that did nothing.

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: the handler of Workspace (names, view, update, run; see deus/workspace.deus)
  signatures:
  - Cli.withWorkspace : Text -> List Text -> (Unit -> {Workspace, IO, Throw Text} a) -> {IO, Throw Text} a
  - Cli.evaluate : Text -> List Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
```

## Requirements

```mdl
req R-1: names lists the names that start with a prefix, and view prints one as deus view does
  by: Workspace.Spec.namesListsPrefix | Workspace.Spec.viewPrintsSource
```

```mdl
req R-2: update changes the codebase as deus update does, and the operations after it see the change
  by: Workspace.Spec.viewSeesUpdate
```

```mdl
req R-3: run runs any deus command against the same codebase
  by: Workspace.Spec.runRunsCommands
```

```mdl
req R-4: deus eval runs its expression with Workspace handled
  by: Workspace.Spec.evaluateHandlesWorkspace
```

## Theorems

The laws are the definitions under `Workspace.Spec`: `deus ls Workspace.Spec.` lists them and `deus view` prints them.
